      "message": "I *think* this program should probably first check that family is ipv4 or ipv6 and otherwise return 1 (allowed), then check protocol is udp/udplite/tcp/sctp/dccp, and otherwise return 1 (allowed).\n\nOtherwise we may potentially run into problems with blocking unix sockets or icmp sockets or raw sockets, etc...\n\nCould write this as a case statement\n\nswitch (ctx-\u003efamily) {\n  case AF_INET:\n  case AF_INET6:\n    break;\n  default:\n    return 1; // not ip -\u003e allowed\n}\n\nswitch (ctx-\u003eprotocol) {\n  case IPPROTO_TCP:  // might need to be wrapped in bpf_htons(IPPROTO_TCP)\n  case IPPROTO_MPTCP: // ?\n  case IPPROTO_UDP/UDPLITE/DCCP/SCTP:\n    break;\n  default:\n    return 1; // unknown protocols are allowed\n}",
